// Oracle question: where may a `;` appear, and does it emit anything?
//
// The original has two productions for it and neither has a semantic action:
// `TopElem -> ;` (`compiler.inc:29`) and `Instr -> Instr ;` (`:149`).  So a
// stray semicolon at the top level is a top-level element that does nothing,
// and one after a statement is part of that statement and does nothing - K65
// is newline-insensitive and the `;` is punctuation an author may write, not
// a separator the language needs.
//
// Both rows had no fixture until G10a and both were "K816 already accepts
// one", asserted by nobody.  Manifest rows `topelem-empty` and
// `instr-semicolon`.

;

const MARK = 0x27 ;

;

data answers { MARK } ;

main {
  a = answers ;
  ;
  return ;
}
